              spacing." Same snap-to-nearest-token convention as
              zimmCartItemActions.css.ts's own `gap: 'var(--zimm-scale-xl)', // Figma: 25px,
              snapped to the nearest token (24px)` comment. */}
          <Text textStyle="body1" color="var(--zimm-color-text-default)">
            {intl.formatMessage(messages.body)}
          </Text>
          <Button
            variant="primary"
            width={{ base: 'full', sm: 'auto' }}
            alignSelf="center"
            onClick={onContinueShoppingClick}
          >
            {intl.formatMessage(messages.continueShopping)}
          </Button>
        </Stack>
      </Center>
    </chakra.div>
  );
};

// --- Decision log -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. No isRegistered branching (body copy or CTA) -- checked session-notes.md §§11.7/11.9/11.10
//    and SFCC-272's actual pulled AC text; none call for a split. See this file's own docblock
//    for the full reasoning. Ready for Marcel to override if SFCC-277's grooming disagrees.
// 2. CTA button included despite neither Figma (figma-reference/empty-bag.md) nor SFCC-272's AC
//    text showing/requesting one -- plan.md step 4.5's own "Changes" text mandates it via the
//    recentlyViewed/EmptyCart structural precedent. Disclosed, not silently assumed.
// 3. Body copy is generic placeholder prose, not the real Figma contact copy -- Marcel's own
//    2026-09-16 decision (session-notes.md §11.9), carried forward to SFCC-277's grooming.
// 4. No outer vertical padding -- no confirmed Figma value; left unset per
//    overrideStyling.md's "leave it inherited... rather than inventing a number," rather than
//    reusing recentlyViewed's own already-disclosed-as-unconfirmed 64px guess.
// 5. Text alignment (centred) is inherited from the mandated Box > Center > Stack precedent
//    structure, not independently confirmed against Figma (the empty-bag.md pull does not state
//    an alignment for the description text block either way). Two separate mechanisms, not one:
//    the outer Stack's own `textAlign="center"` centres the text node, and the Button's own
//    `alignSelf="center"` is what actually centres it as a flex item within that Stack --
//    `textAlign` alone does not position a flex child.
// 6. CTA click closes the drawer and does NOT navigate -- Marcel's direct instruction,
//    2026-09-21, correcting this file's own first attempt (close-and-still-navigate). The CTA
//    dropped `as={Link}`/`href` entirely and is now a plain Button whose only effect is calling
//    `onContinueShoppingClick`; see this file's own "plain Button, not as={Link}" docblock note.

